1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,014
Today's car isn't just a machine.

2
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:06,907
It's a computer, an engine and sensors — working as one.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,813
Early cars were mostly mechanical.

4
00:00:09,853 --> 00:00:14,447
Then came electronics: fuel injection, ABS and airbags.

5
00:00:14,487 --> 00:00:17,260
Now, cars are becoming intelligent.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:21,160
At its core is the ECU — the Electronic Control Unit.

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,725
It reads sensor data,

8
00:00:22,765 --> 00:00:27,260
then controls the engine, transmission and more — in milliseconds.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,609
The same intelligence powers safety:

10
00:00:29,649 --> 00:00:32,759
360° cameras, blind spot monitoring,

11
00:00:32,799 --> 00:00:34,984
lane detection and ADAS.

12
00:00:35,024 --> 00:00:37,651
Availability varies by model.

13
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,394
Proton is part of this shift.

14
00:00:41,434 --> 00:00:44,862
Models like the e.MAS 7 and X50 Flagship

15
00:00:44,902 --> 00:00:48,420
offer 360° cameras and driver assistance.

16
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:51,260
Check the official specs for each variant.

17
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,928
Smarter cars mean safer journeys.

18
00:00:53,968 --> 00:00:56,084
The future of driving is here.

19
00:00:56,124 --> 00:00:59,640
Follow BANG TAF for more automotive insights.
